    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0030" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.24/140</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 830</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-09">August 9, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your
                    strictly confidential telegram no. 158 dated May 17, in section B of which you
                    refer to the desire of the President of Colombia to formalize through an
                    exchange of notes the recommendations made by the General Staffs of Colombia and
                    the United States in pursuance of the staff conversations held in <pb
                        facs="0031" n="23" xml:id="pg23"/> Bogotá in September 1940. This exchange
                    would be submitted to the Colombian Congress for the latter’s approval during
                    its debates on the Convention signed at the Meeting of Foreign Ministers held in
                    Habana in July 1940.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d21-f1"/></p>
                <p>In pursuance of this request, the Department has prepared a draft of this
                        note<anchor n="46" xml:id="d21-f2"/> which you are authorized to submit to
                    President Santos for an expression of his views. The text has received the
                    approval of the War and Navy Departments. You will please keep the Department
                    informed concerning your conversations with the President of Colombia and report
                    any alterations which he may desire to make in the text.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d21-a1.xml" xpointer="d21-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
